.TH CTRL-EXEC-DISPATCHER 8 "2026-06-10" "ctrl-exec" "ctrl-exec Manual"
.SH NAME
ctrl-exec-dispatcher \- mTLS remote script execution control host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctrl-exec-dispatcher
.I mode
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ]
.br
.B ced
.I mode
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctrl-exec-dispatcher
runs on the control host. It manages the private certificate authority,
the agent registry, pairing, certificate rotation, and dispatch of commands
to paired agents over HTTPS with mutual certificate authentication.
.PP
.B ced
is a shortcut for
.BR ctrl-exec-dispatcher .
.SH MODES
.TP
.BI "run " "host[:port] [host...] script " [ "\-\- arg..." ]
Run an allowlisted script on one or more agents in parallel. A host argument
matching a registered agent is resolved from the registry (address and port);
others are used verbatim. Everything after
.B \-\-
is passed to the script.
.TP
.BI "ping " "host[:port] [host...]"
Test mTLS connectivity and report certificate expiry and agent version.
.TP
.B pairing-mode
Accept agent pairing requests interactively on port 7444.
.TP
.B list-requests
Show pending pairing requests.
.TP
.BI "approve " reqid
Approve a pending request. Accepts
.BI \-\-lookup-by " ip|hostname"
and
.BI \-\-agent-port " n"
to set how dispatch reaches the agent.
.TP
.BI "deny " reqid
Deny a pending request.
.TP
.B list-agents
List registered agents. Accepts
.BI \-\-tags " key=value[,key=value...]"
to filter on registry-cached tags (AND), and
.B \-\-json
for machine output.
.TP
.BI "edit-agent " name
Edit a registered agent without re-pairing:
.BI \-\-rename " new"
.RB "/ " \-\-ip
.RB "/ " \-\-agent-port
.RB "/ " \-\-lookup-by .
.TP
.BI "unpair " hostname
Remove a paired agent from the registry.
.TP
.B setup-ca
One-time certificate authority initialisation.
.TP
.B setup-ctrl-exec
Generate the control-host key and certificate.
.TP
.B rotate-cert
Rotate the control-host certificate and broadcast the new serial.
.TP
.B serial-status
Show the control-host serial and per-agent serial state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Path to
.BR ctrl-exec.conf .
Default:
.IR /etc/ctrl-exec/ctrl-exec.conf .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
Override the agent port (7443) for all hosts in this invocation.
.TP
.BI \-\-username " name"
Advisory username in the request context, forwarded to auth hooks.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " token"
Auth token in the request context (default:
.BR $ENVEXEC_TOKEN ).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output results as JSON.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ctrl-exec/ctrl-exec.conf
Control-host configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/ctrl-exec/auth-hook
Optional executable authorising
.B run
and
.B ping
requests.
.TP
.I /var/lib/ctrl-exec
CA, agent registry, pairing queue, locks, and run results.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctrl-exec-agent (8),
.BR ctrl-exec-api (8).
.PP
Full reference: the REFERENCE document shipped with ctrl-exec and
.UR https://github.com/OpenDigitalCC/ctrl-exec
.UE .
